/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  curate23_vp_diethylethanolamine -- the vapour pressure of diethylethanolamine, REFITTED to
  measurements (DEV.md 4c C281 and C283).  Written by `bin/choupo-curate vp
  diethylethanolamine`; everything above the RESULT paragraph is the DECLARATION,
  committed before any fit ran, so it can be read against the result.

  WHY.  The catalogue record carried `vaporPressure { model AmbroseWalton; }`,
  a corresponding-states ESTIMATE from Tc, Pc and omega that never reads the
  record's own Tb (C279 measured a median 19.6 % AAD over the 25 such records
  with archive data).  Here a three-parameter Antoine is fitted to EVERY
  usable laboratory's measurements of it.

  STUDIES (one per article, extracted by `choupo-thermoml extract-vp`; ranked
  by points, ties by DOI):
      10.1021/je049761y                31 pts  278.2-318.3 K  Kapteina; Slovik; Verevkin; Heintz
      10.1016/j.fluid.2018.05.032      24 pts  273.64-308.15 K  Soares; Stejfa; Ferreira; Pinho et al.
      10.1021/je101259r                13 pts  333.2-449.5 K  Klepacova; Huttenhuis; Derks; Versteeg
  SET ASIDE BY NAME:
      10.1021/je301219c: 2 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1021/je4008712: 2 pressure point(s), fewer than 5

  FIT AND ACCEPTANCE (DEV.md 4c C283, Vitor 2026-11-10, declared before the fit).
  EVIDENCE: every study above is fitted; none is held out (C283 amended:
  laboratories disagree with each other by more than they claim, so the
  test is agreement across all of them, not one laboratory's claimed
  precision).  OBJECTIVE: `objective { method twoStage; }` -- least
  squares in log10 P for a first estimate, then the LARGEST relative error in
  P, (P_model - P)/P, over the kept points minimised from it (Vitor's
  practice, C280); both answers kept.  OUTLIERS: after the least-squares
  stage a point with a relative P error above 15 % (three times
  the acceptance) is DISCARDED BY NAME (its study DOI, T and P), listed in
  the result and the record, and the fit repeated without it, once
  (`outliers { maxRelativeError 15 percent; }`).  ACCEPTANCE,
  the DEFAULT of C283: ACCEPTED and promoted (autoPromoted, humanReviewed
  false) when the maximum relative P error over all kept points is at most
  5 % and the normal-boiling-point condition below holds with an
  absolute error below 1 K.  This case declares no
  `system/curationDict`, so the default applies; a case that needs another
  acceptance declares it there, with its reason.  The AmbroseWalton curve's
  errors on the same points are reported beside the fit's, as information.

  NORMAL BOILING POINT: the record's Tb 434.15 K is judged against the range of the KEPT points (all studies span 273.64-449.5 K before any outlier is discarded): if Tb lies OUTSIDE that range, the fitted Antoine's own normal boiling point (P = 101.325 kPa) must lie within the acceptance's temperature error of it, or the gap is announced and the fit is not promoted; inside it, the gap is reported and is not a condition.

  EARLIER FITS, SUPERSEDED BY THIS DECLARATION
  @@EARLIER-BEGIN@@
  C281 step 2, objective leastSquares (log10 P), the same partition and
  band: WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  Antoine log10(Psat/bar) = 5.211269 - 1996.8790/(T + -43.7040),
  in-sample R2 0.999590 over 31 points, 278.2-318.3 K. HELD OUT: 24
  points, AAD 3.5664 % against the band 1.7 % -> notValidated. Its own
  normal boiling point (101.325 kPa): 427.31 K. NOT PROMOTED: held-out
  verdict notValidated (AAD 3.566 % against the band 1.7 % declared
  before the fit); the record keeps AmbroseWalton THEN C281 step 3,
  objective twoStage, one study fitted and one held out, judged by the
  band (superseded by C283): WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`;
  measured, not argued). Objective twoStage. Antoine log10(Psat/bar) =
  5.890606 - 2328.2686/(T + -24.9514), in-sample R2 0.999276 over 31
  points, 278.2-318.3 K. HELD OUT: 24 points, AAD 2.6854 % (max 3.5181 %)
  against the band 1.7 % -> notValidated; the stage-1 least-squares
  answer on the same points: AAD 3.5664 %, max 3.8501 %. Its own normal
  boiling point (101.325 kPa): 420.59 K. NOT PROMOTED: held-out verdict
  notValidated (AAD 2.685 % against the band 1.7 % declared before the
  fit); the record keeps AmbroseWalton
  @@EARLIER-END@@

  NO MEASURED POINT IS IN THIS TREE: constant/archiveDatasets declares every
  series by DOI, NIST URL and sha256; `bin/choupo-curate fetch` regenerates
  them into constant/archiveExtracts/ (gitignored).

  RESULT
  @@RESULT-BEGIN@@
  WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  Objective twoStage. Antoine log10(Psat/bar) = 4.618992 - 1719.9713/(T +
  -61.0754), in-sample R2 0.999872 over 68 kept points, 273.64-449.5 K
  (10.1021/je049761y 31/31 kept; 10.1016/j.fluid.2018.05.032 24/24 kept;
  10.1021/je101259r 13/13 kept). Relative error in P over the kept
  points: mean 2.1349 %, max 3.4740 %; AmbroseWalton on the same points:
  mean 84.4745 %, max 93.2983 %. Outliers discarded: none. Its own normal
  boiling point (101.325 kPa): 433.91 K. PROMOTED on 2026-11-10 into
  data/standards/components/diethylethanolamine.dat as reviewStatus
  autoPromoted, humanReviewed false, because: under the DEFAULT
  acceptance of DEV.md 4c C283 (no system/curationDict), 3 studies, 68
  points kept, 0 discarded as outliers; max relative error 3.474 % (mean
  2.135 %) against 5 %; Tb inside the kept points' range, normal boiling
  point 433.91 K, -0.24 K from the record's Tb 434.15 K (reported, not a
  condition); AmbroseWalton on the same points mean 84.47 % / max 93.3 %
  @@RESULT-END@@
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name       fit_antoine;
        type       vaporPressureFit;
        component  diethylethanolamine;

        evidence
        (
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/diethylethanolamine-vapourPressure-je049761y.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1021/je049761y"; }
                role      fit;
            }
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/diethylethanolamine-vapourPressure-j.fluid.2018.05.032.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1016/j.fluid.2018.05.032"; }
                role      fit;
            }
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/diethylethanolamine-vapourPressure-je101259r.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1021/je101259r"; }
                role      fit;
            }
        );

        objective  { method twoStage; }
        outliers   { maxRelativeError 15 percent; }

        output     { file fit_antoine.csv; }
    }
);
